<!-- Content-Security-Policy as a <meta> element, because GitHub Pages serves
     static files and cannot set response headers. A meta CSP is genuinely
     weaker than the header: `frame-ancestors`, `report-uri` and `sandbox` are
     IGNORED in meta form (w3c CSP3 §3.3), and it applies only after the parser
     reaches it. It still stops an injected external script or an exfiltrating
     `connect-src`, which is the realistic risk for a docs site, so it is worth
     having while being honest that the site cannot carry the full header set —
     documented on the security page. `unsafe-inline` is required: mdBook emits
     inline theme/sidebar scripts and inline styles of its own. -->
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FerroHEALTH/FerroEHR/; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'">
<meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin">
<!-- Self-hosted KaTeX stylesheet (fonts under katex/fonts/) — the site
     serves no external requests, so mdbook-katex runs with no-css = true
     and the vendored sheet is linked here. Version 0.16.4, matching the
     KaTeX the katex-rs renderer inside mdbook-katex bundles (its
     KATEX-VERSION file); provenance in website/book/KATEX-PROVENANCE.md. -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ path_to_root }}katex/katex.min.css">
